            <div xml:id="d782">

                <pb facs="0864" n="854" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg854"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/11–2948: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-29T14:00:00+08:00">November 29,
                            1948—2 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 29—7:04 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2355. French Ambassador informs us in most strict confidence that Vice Foreign
                    Minister George Yeh told him informally that he had been charged with arranging
                    for transportation and accommodation of Diplomatic Corps when Government moves
                    to new capital. He was either unaware or would not reveal place to which
                    Government plans to remove. As this is first intimation of realization that
                    Government may have to move, we are investigating and hope report further.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
